    "description": "Iran’s physical geography combines mountain belts, interior basins, desert surfaces, and coastal lowlands. Their relationships help explain regional differences in drainage, vegetation, and the availability of water. [s1][s2]",
    "tags": ["Physical geography", "Landforms", "Mountain belts", "Drainage", "Deserts"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "ready_for_review",
